<title id="_c9d378cb-02ee-c7ff-c7fb-21879147da9b" semx-id="_741476d2-5b99-d36a-626c-b319c67e05cc">Per-language tpkg bindings</title><fmt-title depth="1" id="_119ec26c-c349-2090-716c-e8dc90555681"><semx element="title" source="_c9d378cb-02ee-c7ff-c7fb-21879147da9b">Per-language tpkg bindings</semx></fmt-title>
<p id="_364041da-7228-bf64-8665-42456962b734" semx-id="_364041da-7228-bf64-8665-42456962b734">The tpkg contract is manipulated per language — never by shelling a foreign binary:  <tt>crates/tpkg</tt> (Rust), <tt>tpkg.h</tt> (C, cbindgen — lands with its first real C consumer),  <tt>tpkg.rb</tt> (Ruby, formalized from the gem's trailer reading).</p>
